1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,193
The decision was taken around a table in the studio, with the minister, the chairman, and the secretary of the embassy all present.

2
00:00:08,193 --> 00:00:12,897
The official from the registrar's office attended by phone.

3
00:00:12,897 --> 00:00:16,956
“We must decide today,” the minister said.

4
00:00:16,956 --> 00:00:28,063
“The obligation is not temporary.” There were six of them around the table, and one empty chair for the volunteer who had resigned.

5
00:00:28,063 --> 00:00:30,853
The general case was simple.

6
00:00:30,853 --> 00:00:41,180
The service would receive a contribution, a negotiation, and a fee; in exchange the team would carry the debt, the penalty, and the marketing.

7
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:45,219
“That is not a partnership,” Maya said.

8
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:56,177
“That is a job with a nicer name.” However, the company had been like this for a month, and the team had to say something.

9
00:00:56,177 --> 00:01:00,971
The expenditure on paper alone was larger than the donation.

10
00:01:00,971 --> 00:01:16,976
A player from the football club, a barber, a cashier, and a secretary from the personnel office came to offer their labor for nothing; a slave in the old architecture of the headquarters building had once done the same for less.

11
00:01:16,976 --> 00:01:21,610
“A vocation is not a penalty,” the chairman said.

12
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:25,565
“Say what you want and we will write it.”

13
00:01:25,565 --> 00:01:30,678
The resignation of the registrar had made the negotiation harder.

14
00:01:30,678 --> 00:01:41,356
The bonus, the retirement plan, the appliance allowance, and the supermarket coupon were all temporary; the work was not.

15
00:01:41,356 --> 00:01:46,140
“I like the sunrise better than the sunset,” Lin said.

16
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:57,667
“I will take the smaller one.” It was likely that the chairman would be angry; it was certain that the team would have to receive the answer together.

17
00:01:57,667 --> 00:02:03,011
In the end they said no to the permanent post and yes to the undertaking.

18
00:02:03,011 --> 00:02:12,324
The headquarters wanted a retirement and got a resignation; the embassy wanted a donation and got a homework club instead.

19
00:02:12,324 --> 00:02:30,859
“There is a commerce in this that is not about money,” Maya wrote, “and there is a service in it that is not about service.” What would happen to the studio was a matter of some interest; so was the question of whether a small undertaking could thrive without a salary.

20
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:37,997
It could, she said, if they were willing to work at sunrise.
